puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen por necesidades distintas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 103 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 16.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.8 to 8.7. December accounts for 18% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 9% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 10. Contract [1], for 14,400 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if the same awardee was used for multiple needs. Review the distribution of contracts across different sectors to ensure no single area was over-purchased.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["B4labwJY6kgUqXM96WStVA%3D%3D","k10KSF6MkNLVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D","D7l0T2gyu1lWhbmkna2nXQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}